# RelativeTime — `ago(ts)` on its own, in a muted span, for the many places a
# row wants an age without wanting the rest of a byline around it: a
# notification, an inbox preview, a stat card's "updated 4h ago". `social/
# PostCard` and `ui/MediaCard` already call `ago()` inline for exactly this; this
# is that same call, extracted, for a caller that has nothing else to put beside
# it.
#
#     use RelativeTime(n.created)
#
# ── `ago` IS A RENDER-TIME BUILTIN, AND THAT COMES WITH A CAVEAT ─────────────
#
# It reads the clock at render time, not at the moment the row was written, so
# the server's first paint and a later client re-render can disagree by however
# long the page has been open — "4h" can become "5h" under the reader without the
# underlying row changing. `live/TimeAgo` is the other answer to the same
# problem: it takes an explicit `asOf` so a host that wants every age on a page
# measured against one instant, and re-measured only when THAT instant changes,
# can seed one. This component is for the common case, which is everywhere this
# library already calls `ago()` directly.
#
# ── NO TOOLTIP, AND THIS FILE CANNOT ADD ONE ─────────────────────────────────
#
# A full date on hover needs a `title` (or equivalent) attribute on the element,
# and no node in this language carries one — only the fixed set each node type
# defines for itself (`alt` on an image, `placeholder` on an input, `poster` on a
# video). `ui/gallery.fct` records the same gap for `alt`. So this renders the
# short form only; a host that needs the exact date on hover is waiting on
# whatever `fct` node eventually carries a generic tooltip attribute, the same
# way a described image is.
app FacetUI:
    css:
        [data-fa-mount] .x-relago { color: var(--fa-muted); font-size: 13px; white-space: nowrap; }
    component RelativeTime(at: int):
        text "{ago(at)}" class "x-relago"
